  "hypothesis": "A head has a repeated-burst response that changes slope with width, a per-burst correction, and a per-train start correction that recurs after a long pause. Pulse width, count and long pauses enter the same transfer law for every lever program on that head. The coefficients and the two optical endpoint forecasts are fixed before any reserved dose.",
  "scoring": "Six pours per head and program. On each of the two sightlines require at least five of six inside max(1.0 nominal mL, 10% of the frozen dose) and absolute mean signed error no greater than max(0.6 nominal mL, 5% of the frozen dose). Require both conditions on both sites for every head and program to call the milestone a pass. Report the stricter individual +/-5% coverage, all residuals and missingness. Unreadable or electrically mismatched attempts count as misses. An unobserved/mismatched receipt fails the corresponding trial. Never replace an initiated wet command on account of its outcome.",
  "secondary_contrasts": {
    "restart": "Compare resumed minus continuous full-opening glass in each matched block. These have the same number and widths of motor pulses; one ordinary interburst gap is extended. Water histories and modeled water volumes differ. Compare measured paired mean difference minus the frozen predicted difference at both sites per head. A 90% paired t interval wholly inside [-1,+1] nominal mL corroborates the restart correction here. Report even on failure.",
    "count": "The brief taste and steady full glass have the same untrained pulse width. Report the observed incremental dose per added burst and compare against the same model. Neither contrast independently identifies a physical cause."
  },
